From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmvcore: Gate the readers' sample times on the writer's files (6522)

The readers' 40 ms video frames and late start on our own files came
from the writer before 6518 (no extended stream properties, a simple
index not counting the preroll); with 6518 both readers give a WMV's
own frame times. This adds the mutation hook for the frame time the
writer puts in the extended stream properties, for the new gate.
---
diff --git a/dlls/wmvcore/asfmux.c b/dlls/wmvcore/asfmux.c
index 9f07f8a..db57a7d 100644
--- a/dlls/wmvcore/asfmux.c
+++ b/dlls/wmvcore/asfmux.c
@@ -300,7 +300,11 @@ static HRESULT build_header(struct asf_mux *mux, struct asf_buffer *out, BOOL fi
         asf_put_dword(out, 0x2);                        /* seekable */
         asf_put_word(out, stream->number & 0x7f);
         asf_put_word(out, 0);                           /* language */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_WMVW_NO_FRAME_TIME
         asf_put_qword(out, stream->time_per_frame);
+#else
+        asf_put_qword(out, 0);
+#endif
         asf_put_word(out, 0);                           /* stream names */
         asf_put_word(out, 0);                           /* payload extension systems */
     }
